*   **C++26 expectations:** The author looks forward to C++26, expecting it to have "stackful coroutines" and "a safe range-based for loop." In the real-world C++ timeline, proposals for a safe range-based for loop (preventing dangling references in loops) gained significant traction and were formally proposed for C++26 in late 2023/early 2024.
*   **Stroustrup’s paper on safety:** The author praises "Stroustrup’s paper on safety" as a "remarkably wise and perceptive document." This refers to Bjarne Stroustrup’s highly controversial September 2023 paper, *"Profiles for safety in C++,"* which was drafted in response to the US government calling out C++ for memory safety issues. By early 2024, this paper was a massive talking point in the C++ community, making it the perfect satirical reference for an April Fools' post.

